---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="WHOlives | Community Transformation Trust" description="Through our partnership with WHOlives, CT Trust supports an innovative loan model that empowers communities to own and maintain their water source for generations.">
  <div class="report-banner-wrap">
    <img class="report-banner" src="/images/projects/wholives.png" alt="" loading="eager" />
  </div>
  <article class="wrap report-article">
    <h1>WHOlives</h1>
    <div class="detail-meta"><span>Ongoing</span><span>Partnership</span></div>
    <p class="detail-lead">Through our partnership with WHOlives, CT Trust supports an innovative loan model that empowers communities to own and maintain their own water source for generations to come.</p>

    <section class="reveal">
      <h3>Water communities can own</h3>
      <p>Rather than giving a well and walking away, this approach helps communities finance, own, and maintain their water source themselves.</p>
      <p>Because the community holds a stake in the outcome, the water source is cared for and kept running for generations, not just for the first few years.</p>
      <img class="report-photo" src="/images/projects/wholives.png" alt="A community-owned water source supported by WHOlives" loading="lazy" />
    </section>

    <section class="reveal">
      <h3>Why the loan model works</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Communities own and maintain their own water source.</li>
        <li>Repaid loans fund the next community&rsquo;s water source.</li>
        <li>Local ownership drives long-term care and sustainability.</li>
        <li>Dignity and self-reliance, not dependency.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="reveal">
      <h3>The lasting difference</h3>
      <p>By supporting a model built on ownership and reinvestment, this partnership creates a cycle of clean water that keeps expanding, generation after generation.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
